        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Calorie needs vary by size and activity level. As a rough guide: a 10 lb senior needs about 200–270 kcal/day, a 40 lb senior needs 540–730 kcal/day, and a 80 lb senior needs 950–1,280 kcal/day. These are estimates for relatively inactive dogs. Use the rib test to monitor body condition: ribs should be easily felt but not visible. Consult your vet for precise calorie targets if your dog has health conditions."
